config BR2_PACKAGE_CAM_SNAP
	bool "cam-snap"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_BAYER2RGB_NEON_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_BAYER2RGB_NEON
	select BR2_PACKAGE_JPEG
	help
	  Single-shot still-image tool for the msm8953 CAMSS pipeline.

	  msm8953 CAMSS only emits raw 10-bit packed Bayer; without any
	  ISP processing the output is heavily green-tinted, washed out,
	  and exposed wrong. cam-snap implements a small software ISP
	  end-to-end:

	    * Set sensor exposure / analogue gain via V4L2 controls
	    * Capture an SGRBG10P frame via mplane mmap
	    * Unpack 10-bit packed → linear 16-bit Bayer
	    * Black-level subtract (64 in 10-bit space)
	    * Gray-world auto white balance (per-channel digital gain)
	    * NEON-accelerated bilinear demosaic via libbayer2rgb-neon
	    * 3x3 sRGB color-correction matrix
	    * Gamma 2.2 + clip to 8-bit RGB
	    * JPEG encode via libjpeg-turbo

	  Output is a viewable JPEG saved to disk. Designed to be called
	  from Elixir (via :ex_camera) so a higher-level layer can drive
	  capture, retries, sensor-control overrides, etc.
